commit d2c7b7a0acadbe1d2367def7fe35514210fbbc0c
Author: Denis Pukinov <denis.pukinov@example.com>
Date:   Sun Jul 19 08:17:12 2026 +0300

    feat: static existence check for AC test locators in review brief (#506)
    
    A valid locator (#505) can still point at a test that does not exist — a silent
    hole. This surfaces it: each verifiable_by=test AC is resolved against the
    project's collected tests and reported in the review brief.
    
    - test_existence.py: collect_test_nodeids (pytest --collect-only, best-effort,
      no test body runs, None when it cannot run) + resolve_ac_locators →
      resolvable / missing / unknown per test-AC
    - models: ACLocatorResolution + ReviewBrief.locator_resolution
    - app: the brief resolves locators only when it has test-AC to check; a missing
      workspace or failed collection yields unknown, never a false missing
    - tests: resolve table (present/absent/no-locator/non-test/unknown), collect
      None-path, and the brief integration with collection mocked
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

